A||||9||86ttops||Running Very Hot||||13||
Z||000000||86ttops||08-16-2001||09:58 AM||||Well the deal basically is that I drive on the highway to work everyday at about 75mph.  The car will run at normal temp for a about 5-10minutes of a 15 minute ride, than the temp rises.  The fan kicks in at 235 like it is suppose to and shuts off at 220 on the gage.  But the temp goes back up again.<BR>  I have had the rediator out of the car there is fluid in the reservoir and no leaks.  I have replaced the fan, coolant temp sensor, water pump(that sucked) and I am pretty sure there isn't any air in the system.  I have no EGR (tube is removed and it is blocked off) but that has been that way for 3-4 years.<P>Any ideas would much appreciated!!||||reg||13
Z||000001||KRMFiero||08-16-2001||10:38 AM||||Try putting in a 160-180 theremistat? or run dual fans on the radiator, one in front, one in back blowing the same way, keep one on constintly with ignition||||reg||1
